      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "Conclusion & Key Takeaways\nPhysics‐inspired message functions drive both significantly lower MAE and strong node/edge correlations.\nLong‐horizon feedback (multi‐step rollouts or lookback windows) and residual predictions prevent error blow‐up over extended forecasts.\nInterpretability metrics reveal when models “cheat” by collapsing latent states—standard MAE alone can be misleading.\nOn real 24‐zone data, our best model (PI_lookback_gradient) achieves 0.5 °C MAE, a 33% improvement over the base MeshGraphNet model (0.75 °C MAE)\n\nFuture Work\nIncorporate occupant behavior and solar gain to the models.\nIntegrate physics‐informed GNNs into an HVAC control systems.\n",
